  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "More equal verbs",
   "texto": [
    "The same is true: **читать** (read), **слушать** (listen), **гулять** (walk), **отдыхать** (rest), and the three meals: **завтракать** (breakfast), **обедать** (lunch) and **ужинать** (dinner).",
    "**Что ты делаешь?** = what are you doing? For formal treatment singular or for several people: **Что вы делаете?**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "When",
   "texto": [
    "The parts of the day are said with one word: **утром** (morning), **днём** (day, noon), **вечером** (afternoon) and **ночью** (evening).",
    "**Сейчас** = now. **Потом** = later.",
    "The Russian present serves current habits and actions: **Я сейчас работаю** can be «I work now.» or «I'm working now.», depending on the context.",
    "An advance of the accusative: many feminine nouns in **-а** change **-у** as a direct object: книга → читаю **книгу**, музыка → слушаю **музыку**. You'll study it calmly in the next chapter."
   ]
